claim:
Data model:
- agent (voice) with a response engine: retell-llm, conversation-flow or custom-LLM WebSocket;
- draft and published versions;
- chat-agent, call (phone/web), chat;
- phone-number with weighted inbound, outbound and SMS agent lists;
- knowledge-base, voice (clone, community), batch-call (create only);
- contact (import, memory, conversations), app (integration connections), CRM config and sync jobs;
- test-case definition, batch test, test run;
- asset, export request (list only), concurrency.
There is no campaign, DNC-list, consent or calling-policy object.

The call object carries:
- disconnection_reason, 39 values, including user_requested_dnc, voicemail_reached, ivr_reached, dial_busy, dial_no_answer, marked_as_spam, scam_detected, credit_exhausted, budget_reached, error_asr;
- per-component latency tracking;
- ProductCost line items in cents per second;
- a public log.
Alerts cover 14 metrics, including call success rate, negative sentiment, transfer failures, QA-not-passed and total cost.

Developer surfaces:
- Custom LLM over WebSocket (llm_websocket_url): the buyer runs the brain, Retell does telephony and turn-taking;
- an MCP server, hosted at mcp.retellai.com and on npm as @retell-ai/mcp-server 6.2.8;
- a CLI, n8n and Zapier nodes, and a ChatGPT app (2026-03-19).

Hosting, from public DNS:
- api.retellai.com: AWS Global Accelerator anycast (13.248.202.14, 3.33.169.178);
- sip.retellai.com: 18.98.16.120-123, AWS us-west-2 EC2;
- mcp.retellai.com: an ELB in us-west-2;
- dashboard and docs: Vercel;
- www: Webflow;
- status: Atlassian Statuspage;
- login: Auth0 custom domain behind Cloudflare.

Marketing and reliability docs claim:
- a 'proprietary voice AI orchestration' and a 'proprietary turn-taking model';
- '~600ms latency';
- 'self-hosted models to reduce third-party dependencies';
- Platform Voices that are 'fine-tuned specifically for conversational AI over the phone';
- a 99.9% uptime guarantee.

Rate card, 2026-10-20:
- voice infra USD 0.055/min;
- TTS 0.015 (Platform, MiniMax, Fish, Cartesia, OpenAI, Inworld) up to 0.10 (ElevenLabs v3 and v4);
- LLM 0.0016-0.32 standard, fast tier up to 0.64 (GPT 6 Astra);
- speech-to-speech gpt-realtime 0.07-0.38;
- telephony: Retell US 0.015, India 0.15 (Twilio) or 0.25 (Telnyx), custom SIP free;
- add-ons: KB, denoise, guardrails +0.005; PII +0.01; AI QA 0.10/min (first 100 min free); batch +0.005/dial; branded call +0.10/call;
- monthly: number 2; concurrency 20 free then 8/slot; KB 10 free then 8 each; verified number 10 (shown as both monthly and one-time).

Billing rules:
- per-second billing; voicemail billed only while the agent is active; failed calls free;
- a 10-second minimum when the agent speaks a dynamic first message;
- prompts over 4,000 tokens scale billed duration by tokens/4,000; the count includes the transcript, tool results and KB chunks;
- concurrency burst +USD 0.10/min for the whole call;
- stable cluster +0.02/min (enterprise);
- since 2026-09-30, prepaid USD credits via Stripe, and calls stop at a zero balance.

Release cadence:
- marketing changelog posts on 2026-05-27, 06-19, 07-02 and 08-24, none since;
- 16 deprecation notices dated 2026-04 to 2026-12;
- 80 retell-sdk npm releases since 2026-04-20 (6.2.8 on 2026-10-17);
- web SDK 3.0.0 on 2026-09-08;
- OpenAPI spec revision dated 2026-10-19.
The API surface changes weekly.

Indian numbers. Retell sells US/CA numbers only, and caller-ID services (branded call, verified number) are US-only, so an Indian CLI needs a BYO elastic SIP trunk or dial-to-SIP. Community threads show the friction:
- Plivo inbound fails with 'user busy' (t/758);
- Plivo Indian numbers are on request; a Retell 'Diamond partner' recommends Vobiz (t/3145);
- a third party says TRAI needs an India-based SBC such as Cloudonix (t/981; unverified);
- TeleCMI IP whitelisting questions (t/842);
- Twilio refuses an India-to-India transfer with caller-ID override (t/2363).

Data handling, per the compliance doc:
- SOC 2 Type 1 and 2; HIPAA (self-signed BAA); GDPR via the AWS DPA;
- zero-data-retention agreements with LLM/ASR/TTS subprocessors (vendor-claimed);
- storage modes: everything / everything_except_pii / basic_attributes_only;
- retention per agent, 1 day to 2 years;
- PII redaction post-call only, 14 US-centric categories (ssn, passport, driver_license and so on; no Aadhaar or PAN);
- signed URLs that expire in 24 h.
Marketing also claims ISO 27001 and 'Enterprise On-prem'; the compliance doc lists neither.

Personalisation:
- dynamic variables per call or CSV column;
- a per-call agent_override;
- contact fields and CRM context read in;
- post-call analysis written back as contact attributes, with backfill across history;
- built-in variables such as current_hour_[timezone].
